      <node id="wilson2008d" label="Notes 1 I use the term 'Norse' throughout: although there were exceptions, most Scandinavian settlers to the Northern Isles came from the region that is now Norway. I also intermittently use the term 'Scandinavian' to denote provenance and origins more generally. he periods 'Viking Age' (c.AD 800-1100) and 'Late Norse' (1100-1300) are referred to as indicators of early or later settlement; otherwise 'Norse' is used as a general indicator of the period of Scandinavian occupation on Orkney. he 'native' Orcadians of the Late Iron Age encountered by the Norse are also known as the 'Picts">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="Notes 1 I use the term 'Norse' throughout: although there were exceptions, most Scandinavian settlers to the Northern Isles came from the region that is now Norway. I also intermittently use the term 'Scandinavian' to denote provenance and origins more generally. he periods 'Viking Age' (c.AD 800-1100) and 'Late Norse' (1100-1300) are referred to as indicators of early or later settlement; otherwise 'Norse' is used as a general indicator of the period of Scandinavian occupation on Orkney. he 'native' Orcadians of the Late Iron Age encountered by the Norse are also known as the 'Picts"/>
          <attvalue for="1" value="2008"/>
